WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.856 align:start position:0% line:0%
Our people cannot sleep
without having soot

00:00:06.856 --> 00:00:08.691 align:start position:0% line:0%
as a thing to worry.

00:00:08.691 --> 00:00:09.560 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's terrible.

00:00:09.560 --> 00:00:11.390 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's actually terrible.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.293 align:start position:0% line:0%
You wake up in the morning
to black particles.

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:18.670
Everyone you meet in Port Harcourt

00:00:18.670 --> 00:00:21.600
has stories about what
they call black soot

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:24.560
caused by the manufacturing
and consumption

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.693
of these fuel products in
the illegal refineries.

00:00:28.890 --> 00:00:31.350
This black soot has been
falling from the sky

00:00:31.350 --> 00:00:35.093
in a region key to Nigeria's
economy for about five years.

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:39.680
Oil theft known as bunkering
and the refining of its spoils

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:41.700 position:56%
is worsening the damage from decades

00:00:41.700 --> 00:00:43.550
of fossil fuel exploitation,

00:00:43.550 --> 00:00:44.560
creating one of the world's

00:00:44.560 --> 00:00:47.650
most severe ecological disasters.

00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:51.320 line:0%
The illegal oil bunkering is a sabotage

00:00:51.320 --> 00:00:53.560 line:0%
to the economy of the nation.

00:00:53.560 --> 00:00:57.957 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's very dangerous to
the health of our people

00:00:57.957 --> 00:01:02.247 align:start position:0% line:0%
and we cannot sit down
and see our people dying.

00:01:03.981 --> 00:01:06.960 line:0%
Our sacred forests, our homes

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:10.000 line:0%
have to give way to oil wells

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:13.260 line:0%
and no one gets much benefit.

00:01:13.260 --> 00:01:14.960
But stealing and refining oil

00:01:14.960 --> 00:01:16.380
is a major source of income

00:01:16.380 --> 00:01:18.370
in a country where wages are meager

00:01:18.370 --> 00:01:20.450 position:63%
and more than half of working age adults

00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:22.723 position:63%
are either unemployed or under employed.

00:01:23.630 --> 00:01:26.060
Many believe that efforts
to stop the illegal trade

00:01:26.060 --> 00:01:28.310
will be in vain and that
the health of the people

00:01:28.310 --> 00:01:31.520
of the Niger Delta will
continue to suffer.

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:34.130 line:0%
Imagine a resident of Port Harcourt

00:01:34.130 --> 00:01:38.800 align:start position:0% line:0%
who inhales this soot
every second in 24 hours,

00:01:38.800 --> 00:01:41.267 line:0%
seven days a week, 30 days in a month

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:43.310 align:start position:0% line:0%
and for years now.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:45.340 line:0%
We are dying slowly but surely

00:01:45.340 --> 00:01:49.047 line:0%
and our lifespan is reducing every day.

00:01:59.938 --> 00:02:00.771
Half a century

00:02:00.771 --> 00:02:02.880
after prospecting began in Nigeria,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:06.573
Shell and BP struck crude in 1956.

00:02:06.573 --> 00:02:09.690
♪ We've been waiting to sell
in bridge Nigeria is spring ♪

00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:11.770
In 1960, when the country declared

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.670 position:58%
independence from the British empire,

00:02:13.670 --> 00:02:16.330
citizens were hopeful that
their newfound resource

00:02:16.330 --> 00:02:18.280 position:61%
would bring prosperity to their nation,

00:02:20.170 --> 00:02:22.430 position:66%
but the years following would be volatile,

00:02:22.430 --> 00:02:26.750
giving away to civil war and a
succession of military coups.

00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:28.940 position:63%
Nevertheless, Nigeria established itself

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:32.513
as a major oil exporter,
but this came at a price.

00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:34.760 line:0%
There have been many, many years

00:02:34.760 --> 00:02:36.640 size:81% position:41% line:0%
in the last 40 or 50 years

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:40.660 align:start position:0% line:0%
where oil sales have
accounted for more than 90%

00:02:40.660 --> 00:02:45.660
of Nigeria's export earnings
and when oil has contributed

00:02:46.200 --> 00:02:49.830
well over 50% of government income,

00:02:49.830 --> 00:02:52.640 position:56%
all this easy money from oil and gas

00:02:52.640 --> 00:02:54.900
meant that the government neglected

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:58.200
other areas of the economy
that should have been key

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:01.160
to Nigeria's development,
such as agriculture,

00:03:01.160 --> 00:03:03.483
basic manufacturing, and mining.

00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:12.470
Aside from oil companies

00:03:12.470 --> 00:03:15.810
and a privileged few Nigerians
in business and politics,

00:03:15.810 --> 00:03:18.420
the country as a whole
has seen minimal benefits

00:03:18.420 --> 00:03:20.673 position:63%
from being Africa's biggest petro state.

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.380 position:58%
One only has to visit the Niger Delta

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:28.170
to see the extent to
which the wealth generated

00:03:28.170 --> 00:03:31.863
by the deposits there has
not been shared equally.

00:03:33.060 --> 00:03:35.230 position:61%
It's a region in which most people live

00:03:35.230 --> 00:03:37.850 position:63%
in really quite impoverished conditions.

00:03:37.850 --> 00:03:41.370 position:58%
There isn't much in way of employment

00:03:41.370 --> 00:03:46.370
and you will not find anyone
who lives in the Delta

00:03:46.700 --> 00:03:50.790
who thinks that their
people have got a fair deal

00:03:50.790 --> 00:03:54.550
out of 60 something
years of oil production.

00:03:55.607 --> 00:03:57.773 size:81% position:41% line:0%
We drink this river water.

00:03:57.773 --> 00:04:00.610 align:start position:0% line:0%
Then if you don't have
money, you drink this water.

00:04:00.610 --> 00:04:03.549 size:84% position:42% line:0%
Then if you have money, you
buy the water and drink.

00:04:03.549 --> 00:04:07.580 position:63%
In the '90s, in a area called Ogoniland,

00:04:07.580 --> 00:04:11.160 align:start position:0% line:0%
a very charismatic activist
called en Saro-wiwa

00:04:11.160 --> 00:04:15.920 align:start position:0% line:0%
launched a campaign against
Shell's operations in the area,

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:18.450 position:58%
accusing it of causing immense levels

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.683
of environmental degradation.

00:04:23.270 --> 00:04:25.760
These demonstrations
caused Shell's operations

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.840
to shut down and exit the area,

00:04:27.840 --> 00:04:30.680
but the activists were met
with swift and violent action

00:04:30.680 --> 00:04:33.613
at the hands of Nigeria's
then-military dictatorship.

00:04:36.210 --> 00:04:38.450
Ledum Mitee is a lawyer, activist,

00:04:38.450 --> 00:04:41.050 position:56%
and survivor of that tumultuous era.

00:04:41.050 --> 00:04:44.950 size:78% position:39% line:0%
Ken and this other of my
colleagues were executed.

00:04:44.950 --> 00:04:49.070 line:0%
I stood trial with Ken and I was lucky

00:04:49.070 --> 00:04:51.923 line:0%
that I was found not guilty and released.

00:04:53.700 --> 00:04:56.440 position:66%
The fate of ken Saro-wiwa and his comrades

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:59.710
laid the path for a violent
backlash in the 2000s

00:04:59.710 --> 00:05:03.010
where militants who preferred
to call themselves agitators

00:05:03.010 --> 00:05:06.120
blew up pipelines, attacked
oil and gas facilities,

00:05:06.120 --> 00:05:07.663
and kidnapped employees.

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:10.007 line:0%
Most times, people I ask them,

00:05:10.007 --> 00:05:13.140 align:start position:0% line:0%
"Why are they resorting
to armed struggle?"

00:05:13.140 --> 00:05:16.200 line:0%
And the people ask me, "Why shouldn't I?

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:19.260 align:start position:0% line:0%
You guys went no- violently
are you were killed.

00:05:19.260 --> 00:05:21.070 line:0%
So we are not gonna wait to be killed

00:05:21.070 --> 00:05:22.967 size:81% position:41% line:0%
before we carry the arms."

00:05:22.967 --> 00:05:25.660 size:78% position:39% line:0%
And that's how militants,

00:05:25.660 --> 00:05:27.733 line:0%
they took over the rest of the region.

00:05:29.400 --> 00:05:31.700 align:start position:0% line:0%
People were angry because
they were not getting

00:05:31.700 --> 00:05:33.570 line:0%
what they thought were their just rewards

00:05:33.570 --> 00:05:35.660 size:88% position:44% line:0%
from the oil from their land

00:05:35.660 --> 00:05:38.593 size:88% position:44% line:0%
and they decided to sabotage
the pipelines and all that.

00:05:47.270 --> 00:05:49.520 position:58%
We met with a former militant leader,

00:05:49.520 --> 00:05:52.950
a former agitator leader who
goes by the nomme de guerre

00:05:52.950 --> 00:05:55.440
of Osama Bin Laden.

00:05:55.440 --> 00:05:58.670 size:78% position:39% line:0%
That name because of what
we used to blow the pipe

00:05:58.670 --> 00:06:00.110 size:75% position:38% line:0%
and do all those things.

00:06:00.110 --> 00:06:01.813 align:start position:0% line:0%
That was our bush name.

00:06:06.660 --> 00:06:07.493 align:start position:0% line:0%
We are suffering.

00:06:07.493 --> 00:06:10.310 line:0%
You will see charcoal everywhere.

00:06:10.310 --> 00:06:11.203 align:start position:0% line:0%
See this thing?

00:06:12.050 --> 00:06:13.920 line:0%
I can see the stain on the clothes.

00:06:13.920 --> 00:06:16.026 line:0%
Our objective that time is that

00:06:16.026 --> 00:06:18.280 size:84% position:42% line:0%
they cannot collect our oil

00:06:18.280 --> 00:06:21.823 line:0%
without making our place okay for us.

00:06:23.221 --> 00:06:24.054 align:start position:0% line:0%
Do you see?

00:06:24.893 --> 00:06:27.020 line:0%
If they're getting the oil from us,

00:06:27.020 --> 00:06:29.513 line:0%
they should make our place fine.

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:34.300 position:66%
The Ogoniland native is one of the leaders

00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:36.980
in a loose coalition of
heavily armed militias

00:06:36.980 --> 00:06:39.550
that carried out a campaign,
which at its height,

00:06:39.550 --> 00:06:43.610
reduced Nigeria's oil
production by up to 40%.

00:06:43.610 --> 00:06:47.227
This violence became so
bad in the late 2000s

00:06:47.227 --> 00:06:49.730 position:58%
and was having such a negative impact

00:06:49.730 --> 00:06:52.570
on Nigeria's daily oil output

00:06:52.570 --> 00:06:57.250
that the then president
offered the main leaders

00:06:57.250 --> 00:07:00.100
and their men an amnesty program.

00:07:00.100 --> 00:07:02.420
The leaders got properties

00:07:02.420 --> 00:07:05.090
and lucrative business
opportunities for disarming

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:08.100
and their men got monthly stipends

00:07:08.100 --> 00:07:10.293 position:58%
which they still receive to this day.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.955
Now he prefers to present
himself as a peacemaker.

00:07:17.755 --> 00:07:20.813 line:0%
This will encourage me to do more

00:07:20.813 --> 00:07:24.108 line:0%
and make sure that the Ogoni people,

00:07:24.108 --> 00:07:26.559 line:0%
all the place have peace, thank you.

00:07:27.837 --> 00:07:31.857 align:start position:0% line:0%
If we lay down our arms,
they will empower us.

00:07:31.857 --> 00:07:34.483 line:0%
They will find job for our boys.

00:07:35.450 --> 00:07:40.383 line:0%
Then they will make sure that
the environment here is okay.

00:07:43.493 --> 00:07:46.450 position:63%
But the environment is anything but okay

00:07:46.450 --> 00:07:48.830
and many of the jobs
that have been created

00:07:48.830 --> 00:07:50.030
are in the black market.

00:07:51.090 --> 00:07:52.140
Much of the crude oil

00:07:52.140 --> 00:07:54.490
that is stolen from pipelines

00:07:54.490 --> 00:07:57.150
makes its way to illegal refineries

00:07:57.150 --> 00:08:00.090 position:56%
that are situated deep in the creeks

00:08:00.090 --> 00:08:02.310
and deep in the forests
of the Niger Delta,

00:08:02.310 --> 00:08:04.950
far from the prying
eyes of the government.

00:08:04.950 --> 00:08:05.880
It's at these sites

00:08:05.880 --> 00:08:08.320
where the entire industry
of illegal refining,

00:08:08.320 --> 00:08:09.930 position:56%
which is commonly known in the Delta

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:12.830
as kpo fire takes place.

00:08:12.830 --> 00:08:14.680
The products that they produce

00:08:14.680 --> 00:08:19.480
in these refining sites
are sold to traders

00:08:19.480 --> 00:08:23.470
who go and sell these products
throughout the Niger Delta

00:08:23.470 --> 00:08:25.890
and throughout the wider country.

00:08:25.890 --> 00:08:27.320
The government currently estimates

00:08:27.320 --> 00:08:31.160
that up to 150,000 barrels
of oil are stolen every day

00:08:31.160 --> 00:08:34.920
equivalent to about 10%
of official production.

00:08:34.920 --> 00:08:36.880 position:63%
Some industry figures estimate the scale

00:08:36.880 --> 00:08:38.503
of the theft is even greater.

00:08:39.770 --> 00:08:41.220 size:84% position:42% line:0%
So what we are seeing today

00:08:42.120 --> 00:08:45.910 line:0%
is the flip side of the same militancy

00:08:45.910 --> 00:08:48.143 line:0%
instead of breaking pipelines,

00:08:49.750 --> 00:08:52.870 align:start position:0% line:0%
just to spite the government
and the oil companies,

00:08:52.870 --> 00:08:55.410 line:0%
we break pipelines to make money

00:08:55.410 --> 00:08:57.033 size:78% position:39% line:0%
through illegal refining.

00:08:59.100 --> 00:09:01.410 position:66%
The tapping of pipelines, stealing of oil,

00:09:01.410 --> 00:09:03.530
and the emissions from
the refining process

00:09:03.530 --> 00:09:05.220
have added another complication

00:09:05.220 --> 00:09:08.630
to the region's environmental
crisis and as expected,

00:09:08.630 --> 00:09:10.510 position:61%
it's affecting the health and wellbeing

00:09:10.510 --> 00:09:11.853
of local inhabitants.

00:09:13.080 --> 00:09:17.250 align:start position:0% line:0%
We first observed these
medical refining issues

00:09:17.250 --> 00:09:19.300 size:75% position:38% line:0%
that culminated into the
appearance of the soot

00:09:19.300 --> 00:09:20.820 line:0%
in Port Harcourt and its metropolis

00:09:20.820 --> 00:09:24.830 size:75% position:38% line:0%
sometime in 2017 when it
became very much visible

00:09:24.830 --> 00:09:28.480 align:start position:0% line:0%
and since then we've been
having issues with respiration,

00:09:28.480 --> 00:09:31.280 align:start position:0% line:0%
issues with the heart,
issues with the liver,

00:09:31.280 --> 00:09:34.250 line:0%
issues with the kidneys of residents

00:09:34.250 --> 00:09:37.210 line:0%
of Port Harcourt and its environments.

00:09:37.210 --> 00:09:39.790 size:88% position:44% line:0%
The complaints are valuable.

00:09:39.790 --> 00:09:40.890 align:start position:0% line:0%
They're not static.

00:09:40.890 --> 00:09:42.353 align:start position:0% line:0%
They are just too many.

00:09:43.195 --> 00:09:44.970 line:0%
And this is what we inhale every day.

00:09:44.970 --> 00:09:47.420 line:0%
If we bathe our body, it's charcoal.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.870 size:78% position:39% line:0%
If we step on the ground,
everywhere is charcoal.

00:09:50.830 --> 00:09:53.000 position:56%
This issue of black soot is not new.

00:09:53.000 --> 00:09:55.200 position:61%
It's been around for a couple of years,

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:57.970
but the governor told
us that he was obliged

00:09:57.970 --> 00:10:00.970 position:66%
to launch his war against illegal refining

00:10:00.970 --> 00:10:03.943 position:59%
because the problem had become so bad.

00:10:04.920 --> 00:10:08.910 line:0%
What we did was from our own vigilante

00:10:10.430 --> 00:10:12.283 size:88% position:44% line:0%
to monitor what is going on.

00:10:13.760 --> 00:10:16.874 line:0%
I cannot tell you here authoritatively

00:10:16.874 --> 00:10:20.053 line:0%
that we have completely stopped.

00:10:20.890 --> 00:10:24.280 line:0%
I can say that we have been able

00:10:25.553 --> 00:10:30.553 align:start position:0% line:0%
to reduce the level of
these illegal activities.

00:10:31.570 --> 00:10:34.603 line:0%
If identify a site, I'll destroy it.

00:10:44.830 --> 00:10:46.400
Since launching his crusade,

00:10:46.400 --> 00:10:47.840
the governor's task force

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.450
claimed to have found and destroyed

00:10:49.450 --> 00:10:52.190
at least 480 of the so-called ovens

00:10:52.190 --> 00:10:54.410
used for cooking the crude oil.

00:10:54.410 --> 00:10:58.140 align:start position:0% line:0%
The governor declared a
total war on illegal refinery

00:10:58.140 --> 00:11:00.340 line:0%
to keep the people of Rivers State alive.

00:11:00.340 --> 00:11:01.800 line:0%
You can't drink from the water.

00:11:01.800 --> 00:11:04.080 line:0%
You can't do anything from this place

00:11:04.080 --> 00:11:07.310 size:84% position:42% line:0%
because of these activities
of illegal oil refineries.

00:11:07.310 --> 00:11:08.143 align:start position:0% line:0%
This is the route.

00:11:08.143 --> 00:11:10.330 line:0%
They bring in their speed boats here.

00:11:10.330 --> 00:11:13.110 align:start position:0% line:0%
On drums and barrels?
Yes, in barrels.

00:11:13.110 --> 00:11:16.253 align:start position:0% line:0%
You can smell oil.
Crude, yes, it's crude.

00:11:17.760 --> 00:11:20.517 line:0%
All our rivers here are gone.

00:11:20.517 --> 00:11:22.870 line:0%
The environment is messed up.

00:11:22.870 --> 00:11:24.429 size:75% position:38% line:0%
We have published names.

00:11:24.429 --> 00:11:26.890 align:start position:0% line:0%
We have also conducting
house to house arrest.

00:11:26.890 --> 00:11:29.010
When we visited a site

00:11:29.010 --> 00:11:31.940
which had recently been
dismantled and destroyed

00:11:31.940 --> 00:11:34.720
by the local government,
it really gave us a sense

00:11:34.720 --> 00:11:37.947 align:start position:0% line:0%
of the size of this industry
in this very small area.

00:11:37.947 --> 00:11:41.467 align:start position:0% line:0%
If we don't destroy the
heart of the activity.

00:11:41.467 --> 00:11:44.810 line:0%
which is the illegal refining centers,

00:11:44.810 --> 00:11:46.613 line:0%
then the crude will be cooked,

00:11:46.613 --> 00:11:48.179 line:0%
the soot will still be in the air,

00:11:48.179 --> 00:11:51.010 line:0%
and you just be scratching the surface.

00:11:51.010 --> 00:11:53.070 align:start position:0% line:0%
We have done what the
governor has told us to do

00:11:53.070 --> 00:11:56.490 line:0%
and it has yielded huge amount of results.

00:11:56.490 --> 00:11:59.090 position:61%
That was one small area in River State.

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:01.470
So if there was that
many ovens just there,

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:04.210
it gives an impression of
how many might be elsewhere

00:12:04.210 --> 00:12:05.393
throughout the Delta.

00:12:16.280 --> 00:12:18.310 position:59%
Fyneface Dumnamene is a local activist

00:12:18.310 --> 00:12:20.940
who spent years fighting
for environmental justice

00:12:20.940 --> 00:12:22.790 position:58%
for the residents of the River State.

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:27.170 align:start position:0% line:0%
The entire Niger Delta
is the most polluted part

00:12:27.170 --> 00:12:30.310 line:0%
of the earth anywhere in the world.

00:12:30.310 --> 00:12:33.980 align:start position:0% line:0%
This community has been
massively polluted by hydrocarbon

00:12:34.870 --> 00:12:37.743 align:start position:0% line:0%
from the activities of
multinational oil companies.

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:42.100 align:start position:0% line:0%
The people of Ogoni are dying
as a result of pollution.

00:12:42.100 --> 00:12:44.340 line:0%
If you test an average Ogoni man,

00:12:44.340 --> 00:12:47.380 line:0%
you will see that he or she has
been polluted in their lungs

00:12:47.380 --> 00:12:49.570 line:0%
because of what they inhale every day

00:12:49.570 --> 00:12:51.720 align:start position:0% line:0%
in the polluted
environment that they live.

00:12:53.070 --> 00:12:56.330 align:start position:0% line:0%
In Niger Delta, we have
well over 40 million people.

00:12:56.330 --> 00:12:58.060 line:0%
23 million of these are young people

00:12:58.060 --> 00:13:00.470 align:start position:0% line:0%
and a lot of these will
have a lesser percentage

00:13:00.470 --> 00:13:02.113 size:84% position:42% line:0%
that are gainfully engaged.

00:13:03.130 --> 00:13:06.230 line:0%
The youth of the Niger Delta have waited

00:13:06.230 --> 00:13:09.160 size:75% position:38% line:0%
for the oil companies to
provide jobs for them.

00:13:09.160 --> 00:13:10.900 line:0%
They are not getting the jobs.

00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:12.840 align:start position:0% line:0%
When they go to them to
seek for opportunities

00:13:12.840 --> 00:13:15.390 size:81% position:41% line:0%
to be able to be employed,
they are not getting it.

00:13:22.580 --> 00:13:24.510 position:58%
Fred Barikpoa says he's been involved

00:13:24.510 --> 00:13:27.680
in the black market of
oil refining since 2016,

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:31.030
but has had to stop due
to the recent crackdown.

00:13:31.030 --> 00:13:33.550
His cousin Favour said
she used to sell the fuel

00:13:33.550 --> 00:13:35.340
and suffers from multiple ailments

00:13:35.340 --> 00:13:38.160 position:59%
that she blames on inhaling oil fumes.

00:13:38.160 --> 00:13:41.407 line:0%
We don't have any means of livelihood.

00:13:41.407 --> 00:13:42.707 size:81% position:41% line:0%
We don't have any support.

00:13:43.990 --> 00:13:46.670 line:0%
Since we don't have any other means,

00:13:46.670 --> 00:13:49.320 align:start position:0% line:0%
we don't have any other
choice than to risk our lives

00:13:51.837 --> 00:13:54.931 align:start position:0% line:0%
and all of my friends are
going into the business more

00:13:54.931 --> 00:13:57.210 align:start position:0% line:0%
and the business is killing
a lot of people more.

00:13:57.210 --> 00:14:00.653 size:84% position:42% line:0%
If you get to the mortuary,
you see what we are saying,

00:14:01.510 --> 00:14:03.134 line:0%
but since we don't have any option,

00:14:03.134 --> 00:14:04.953 align:start position:0% line:0%
we are going into the
business that is killing us.

00:14:10.440 --> 00:14:13.790 align:start position:0% line:0%
You can see my sister,
Favour, they are suffering

00:14:13.790 --> 00:14:17.128 size:84% position:42% line:0%
because I have no option
than to go for the business

00:14:17.128 --> 00:14:19.461 size:88% position:44% line:0%
for her to sustain a little.

00:14:21.112 --> 00:14:25.678 align:start position:0% line:0%
When this thing started,
I cannot stand it.

00:14:25.678 --> 00:14:28.195 line:0%
I cannot do anything in here.

00:14:28.195 --> 00:14:33.059 align:start position:0% line:0%
So I am praying, pleading
for the government.

00:14:33.059 --> 00:14:36.600 line:0%
They should do something about it.

00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:38.483 align:start position:0% line:0%
When I saw the woman,
she's having Anasarca.

00:14:38.483 --> 00:14:41.240 line:0%
That means that generalized body swelling.

00:14:41.240 --> 00:14:42.890 line:0%
There has been oil spills there before?

00:14:42.890 --> 00:14:44.020 align:start position:0% line:0%
Everywhere.
Everywhere?

00:14:44.020 --> 00:14:46.952 line:0%
A lot of these kpo fire thing?

00:14:46.952 --> 00:14:48.200 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's everywhere.

00:14:48.200 --> 00:14:49.920 align:start position:0% line:0%
It's all everywhere.

00:14:49.920 --> 00:14:52.580 size:78% position:39% line:0%
If you look at the woman,
she could hardly breathe.

00:14:52.580 --> 00:14:53.720 align:start position:0% line:0%
She couldn't walk

00:14:53.720 --> 00:14:58.523 line:0%
because her heart is failing.
Congestive cardiac failure.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.570 align:start position:0% line:0%
She has the classical
features of almost all,

00:15:02.570 --> 00:15:06.210 size:84% position:42% line:0%
all the major complications
of the soot is manifest.

00:15:06.210 --> 00:15:10.380 size:88% position:44% line:0%
We want to check your heart,
your liver, and your kidney.

00:15:15.944 --> 00:15:19.690 align:start position:0% line:0%
Help me and get me out of this
trouble and this sickness.

00:15:24.322 --> 00:15:27.406 align:start position:0% line:0%
I still want to live.

00:15:27.406 --> 00:15:29.928 line:0%
I have children to take care of.

00:15:29.928 --> 00:15:34.928 line:0%
I have family to take care of.

00:15:48.120 --> 00:15:51.460 align:start position:0% line:0%
The life span of residents
of Port Harcourt,

00:15:51.460 --> 00:15:54.250 line:0%
it is reducing and it will keep reducing

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.510 line:0%
far as long as we still breathe in

00:15:56.510 --> 00:15:59.770 line:0%
this polluted air occasioned by the soot.

00:16:03.107 --> 00:16:05.190
According to Amnesty International,

00:16:05.190 --> 00:16:08.220
hundreds of oil spills occur
in the Niger Delta every year

00:16:08.220 --> 00:16:10.980 position:63%
and they are rarely properly cleaned up.

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:13.540
While most go unnoticed
by the outside world,

00:16:13.540 --> 00:16:16.163
two recent incidents did
capture public attention.

00:16:18.330 --> 00:16:22.010
In November 2021, a well
exploded, spewing oil and gas

00:16:22.010 --> 00:16:24.370
into the surrounding
rivers and mangrove swamps

00:16:24.370 --> 00:16:26.120
for almost 40 days.

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:28.593
A meaningful cleanup
has yet to take place.

00:16:32.600 --> 00:16:33.560
A few months later,

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.880
a storage tanker blew up
just off Nigeria's coast.

00:16:36.880 --> 00:16:38.170
The environment ministry says

00:16:38.170 --> 00:16:40.563
it was holding up to
60,000 barrels of oil.

00:16:41.460 --> 00:16:44.820 align:start position:0% line:0%
The environment has been
irredeemably damaged

00:16:45.730 --> 00:16:47.340 line:0%
and yet nothing is happening.

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:48.730 line:0%
Nobody has been held to account.

00:16:48.730 --> 00:16:50.910 line:0%
No government official has been sacked.

00:16:50.910 --> 00:16:53.230 line:0%
No action has been taken with respect to,

00:16:53.230 --> 00:16:54.860 line:0%
you know, holding people accountable

00:16:54.860 --> 00:16:58.387 size:81% position:41% line:0%
for failure to take care
of their responsibilities.

00:17:00.648 --> 00:17:03.870
In 2010, the United
Nations Environment Program

00:17:03.870 --> 00:17:06.830
produced a report about oil
spills' environmental damage

00:17:06.830 --> 00:17:10.260
in the Ogoniland, recommending
a five-year cleanup project

00:17:10.260 --> 00:17:12.530 position:58%
estimated to cost one billion dollars

00:17:12.530 --> 00:17:14.483
and funded primarily by Shell.

00:17:15.740 --> 00:17:16.660
A government agency

00:17:16.660 --> 00:17:19.410
called the Hydrocarbon
Pollution Remediation Project

00:17:19.410 --> 00:17:22.450
or HYPREP has been put in
charge of the cleanup effort

00:17:22.450 --> 00:17:25.263 position:63%
and awarded its first contracts in 2018.

00:17:26.310 --> 00:17:29.270
While HYPREP does publish
regular activity updates,

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:31.280 position:66%
Ogoniland residents claim not to have seen

00:17:31.280 --> 00:17:33.313
substantial progress as of yet.

00:17:35.360 --> 00:17:37.030 position:63%
12 years later, there's a lot of concern

00:17:37.030 --> 00:17:38.520
about the progress of the project

00:17:38.520 --> 00:17:40.830 position:64%
and activist groups, environmental groups

00:17:40.830 --> 00:17:43.390 position:61%
accused the people managing the project

00:17:43.390 --> 00:17:46.690 align:start position:0% line:0%
of not operating in a
particularly transparent way.

00:17:46.690 --> 00:17:51.530 size:81% position:41% line:0%
We had a lot of hope and
some sense of satisfaction

00:17:51.530 --> 00:17:53.833 line:0%
that at least we have achieved something,

00:17:54.950 --> 00:17:58.350 line:0%
but several years after, I'm afraid that

00:17:58.350 --> 00:18:00.283 line:0%
I cannot say that there's a cleanup.

00:18:01.320 --> 00:18:04.370
They haven't even finished
cleaning up the sites

00:18:04.370 --> 00:18:09.370
that were classified as simple
and are yet to even give out

00:18:09.510 --> 00:18:14.210
the contracts to clean up the
areas categorized as complex.

00:18:14.210 --> 00:18:15.360
HYPREP did not respond

00:18:15.360 --> 00:18:17.143
to several requests for comment.

00:18:18.480 --> 00:18:19.910 line:0%
Not much have been achieved in Ogoni

00:18:19.910 --> 00:18:21.920 line:0%
that was supposed to serve as a model

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:23.640 line:0%
for other parts of the Niger Delta

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:25.420 size:84% position:42% line:0%
and I think they need to go
back to the drawing board

00:18:25.420 --> 00:18:28.190 align:start position:0% line:0%
and be able to carry out the
environmental remediation

00:18:28.190 --> 00:18:30.748 align:start position:0% line:0%
of Ogoni and then extend it
to other parts of River States

00:18:30.748 --> 00:18:31.940 line:0%
and other parts of the Niger Delta

00:18:31.940 --> 00:18:33.950 align:start position:0% line:0%
because if they keep
delaying this process,

00:18:33.950 --> 00:18:37.620 align:start position:0% line:0%
the lifespan of an average
Ogoni Rivers man and Delta man

00:18:37.620 --> 00:18:39.580 line:0%
will continue to reduce because we live

00:18:39.580 --> 00:18:42.343 align:start position:0% line:0%
in polluted environment
every day of our lives.

